price = 19.999
print(round(price, 2))

price = 4.5
print(f"Price: ${price:.2f}")

total = 10.129
print(round(total, 2))
print(f"{total:.2f}")
Both lines print 10.13, but only one of them actually changes the value it uses.
round(total, 2) → creates a new rounded number (like 10.13). If you did total = round(total, 2), then total itself would change.
f"{total:.2f}" → keeps total the same inside Python, but formats it to look like 10.13 when printed
